var LIMITS=" The name does not verify amount, purity, exact composition or grade, feedstock, manufacturing process, or allergy cross-contact.",CONTEXT="An emulsifying or texture function is not a health benefit. Permission or inventory listing does not establish that this product complies with use conditions or is safe for an individual. Findings for one emulsifier, cellulose form, laboratory preparation, or drug/supplement exposure are not automatically findings for another or for this food. Existing health-evidence records, colors, and review dates are unchanged.";
var data=[[["lecithin","lecithins"],"Emulsifier · source unspecified","Lecithin is a phospholipid-rich mixture, not one pure compound. Generic wording does not identify the ingredient source; soy or sunflower origin must not be inferred.","May help ingredients mix or remain dispersed. The name does not establish the manufacturer's purpose or meaningful choline intake.","184.1400",true],[["soy lecithin","soya lecithin"],"Emulsifier · soy stated","The label names soy as the stated source of a lecithin preparation. This is not independent verification of manufacture, residual protein, or allergy safety.","May help ingredients mix or remain dispersed. A technical use does not cancel a saved soy-allergy warning or establish a nutritional benefit.","184.1400",false],[["sunflower lecithin"],"Emulsifier · sunflower stated","The label names sunflower as the stated source of a lecithin preparation. It does not verify manufacture, composition, or absence of other allergens.","May help ingredients mix or remain dispersed. The label does not establish dietary certification, the exact function, or a health benefit.","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7010002/",false],[["mono- and diglycerides","mono and diglycerides","mono & diglycerides","mono- and diglycerides of fatty acids"],"Emulsifier / formulation aid","A mixture of glycerol esters of fatty acids. Plant versus animal origin and the mono/diglyceride ratio are not established by this wording.","May emulsify, stabilize, condition dough, or assist formulation. Do not infer vegan or vegetarian suitability from the chemical name.","184.1505",true],[["polysorbate 20","polyoxyethylene (20) sorbitan monolaurate"],"Surface-active ingredient","A specifically named polysorbate preparation, distinct from polysorbate 60 or 80 and from unmodified sorbitan esters.","Can help disperse or distribute ingredients. FDA inventory spans technical contexts, not blanket authorization for every direct food use; the manufacturer's actual role is unknown.","https://www.hfpappexternal.fda.gov/scripts/fdcc/index.cfm?set=FoodSubstances&id=POLYSORBATE20",false],[["polysorbate 60","polyoxyethylene (20) sorbitan monostearate"],"Emulsifier / formulation aid","A named polysorbate preparation associated with stearate/palmitate esters. It is not polysorbate 80 or sorbitan monostearate.","May emulsify, disperse, or affect formulation in specified food uses. The label does not establish compliance with food-specific conditions.","172.836",false],[["polysorbate 80","polyoxyethylene (20) sorbitan monooleate"],"Emulsifier / dispersing agent","A named polysorbate preparation associated with oleate esters. It is not polysorbate 60; findings are not automatically interchangeable.","May emulsify, solubilize, disperse, or serve other specified technical functions. The name does not establish this product's amount or use.","172.840",false],[["sorbitan monostearate"],"Emulsifier / formulation aid","A sorbitan ester preparation described as a mixture of partial stearate/palmitate esters. It is distinct from polysorbate 60.","May emulsify specified foods or assist rehydration and other specified uses. Fatty-acid origin and dietary suitability are not established by the name.","172.842",false],[["sodium stearoyl lactylate","sodium stearoyl-2-lactylate"],"Emulsifier / dough conditioner","A mixture of sodium salts of stearoyl lactylic and related acids, not simply sodium lactate. The name does not establish fatty-acid origin.","May condition dough, emulsify, stabilize, or assist texture in specified uses. It does not establish meaningful sodium supplementation.","172.846",false],[["calcium stearoyl lactylate","calcium stearoyl-2-lactylate"],"Dough conditioner / whipping aid","A mixture of calcium salts of stearoyl lactylic and related acids, distinct from the sodium preparation.","May condition dough, assist whipping, or serve other specified functions. It does not establish meaningful calcium supplementation or a health benefit.","172.844",false],[["methylcellulose","methyl cellulose"],"Cellulose derivative / texture agent","A methyl-substituted cellulose preparation, not CMC or hydroxypropyl methylcellulose. The viscosity and substitution grade are not established.","May emulsify, stabilize, or thicken foods. Findings for dry medicinal products must not be transferred automatically to this food.","https://www.hfpappexternal.fda.gov/scripts/fdcc/index.cfm?set=FoodSubstances&id=CELLULOSEMETHYL",false],[["hydroxypropyl methylcellulose","hydroxypropyl methyl cellulose","hpmc","hypromellose"],"Cellulose derivative / texture agent","A specifically named cellulose ether preparation, not methylcellulose, hydroxypropyl cellulose, or CMC.","May emulsify, form films, stabilize, suspend, or thicken specified formulations. A capsule-coating use does not establish this product's purpose.","172.874",false],[["hydroxypropyl cellulose","hydroxypropylcellulose","hpc"],"Cellulose derivative / texture agent","A hydroxypropyl-substituted cellulose preparation. Generic wording does not identify substitution or viscosity grade, including low-substituted preparations.","Technical functions depend on grade and use; they can include emulsification, film formation, stabilization, thickening, or binding. They are not a digestive-health claim.","172.870",false],[["microcrystalline cellulose","cellulose gel","mcc"],"Cellulose preparation / formulation aid","A microcrystalline cellulose preparation, distinct from powdered cellulose and cellulose gum/CMC. Blended preparations are not inferred.","FDA lists formulation, moisture-retention, stabilizing, thickening, and other technical functions. The label does not establish exact use or a fiber benefit.","https://www.hfpappexternal.fda.gov/scripts/fdcc/index.cfm?set=FoodSubstances&id=CELLULOSEMICROCRYSTALLINE",false],[["powdered cellulose","cellulose powder"],"Cellulose preparation / formulation aid","A powdered cellulose preparation, not silently equated with microcrystalline cellulose or chemically modified cellulose derivatives.","May contribute bulk or affect texture and formulation. Specifications and permitted uses vary by jurisdiction; no universal authorization or health benefit is inferred.","https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.2903/j.efsa.2018.5047",false],[["cellulose"],"Cellulose · preparation unspecified","Generic cellulose wording does not identify powdered, microcrystalline, or a named modified derivative. Those preparations must not be inferred.","A cellulose-associated ingredient that may affect bulk or texture. Its exact preparation, function, and nutritional contribution are unspecified.","https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.2903/j.efsa.2018.5047",true]];
