var LIMITS=" The label does not establish amount, batch certification, purity, carriers, particle characteristics, manufacturing date, or compliance in the market where this product is sold.",CONTEXT="A coloring function is not a health benefit. Synthetic, plant-derived, mineral, or certification-exempt wording is not a universal safety verdict or proof of allergy safety. Food, drug, and cosmetic permissions are not interchangeable. Existing health-evidence records and colors are unchanged; this is not a new clinical or product assessment.",POLICY="As checked 2026-10-11, FDA describes working with industry to eliminate the six remaining commonly used certified dyes by the end of 2027. This initiative and company pledges are not proof that every product is reformulated or a blanket completed legal ban. Check current rules and the actual market/product.",REDPOLICY="As checked 2026-10-11, FDA revoked Red No. 3 authorization with reformulation deadlines of January 15, 2027 for food and January 18, 2028 for ingested drugs. FDA says products manufactured before the effective date may still be encountered afterward. A label name alone does not establish manufacture date, illegality, or a human health outcome.";
