var LIMITS=" The wording does not verify amount, full formulation, carriers, manufacturing route, residual alcohol, dietary certification, or allergy cross-contact.",CONTEXT="Natural and artificial are labeling categories, not health or safety grades. Generic terms do not disclose every component or establish vegan, organic, alcohol-free, or allergy-safe status. A listed technical use is not a clinical benefit or product-compliance verdict. Existing health-evidence records, colors, review dates, and allergy/diet rules are unchanged.";
var data=[[["natural flavor","natural flavors","natural flavour","natural flavours","natural flavoring","natural flavorings","natural flavouring","natural flavourings"],"Flavor category · components unspecified","Under US rules, natural flavor is defined by specified source materials and a principally flavoring function. Permitted source materials include plant and animal foods and fermentation products; natural does not mean plant-only or unprocessed.","A category for ingredients whose principal function is flavoring rather than nutrition. Specific components, amounts, and this preparation's source are not established.","101.22",true,"US 21 CFR 101.22 permits certain collective flavor/spice declarations but separately requires names for added MSG and protein hydrolysates. Applicable major-allergen labeling obligations still apply. The app does not verify that this database record or package meets those rules."],[["artificial flavor","artificial flavors","artificial flavour","artificial flavours","artificial flavoring","artificial flavorings","artificial flavouring","artificial flavourings"],"Flavor category · components unspecified","Under US rules, artificial flavor covers flavor-imparting substances not derived from the specified natural-source categories. The phrase does not identify individual chemicals or their manufacturing details.","A category for flavoring ingredients. Artificial wording does not by itself establish harm, benefit, composition, or suitability for an individual.","101.22",true,"US 21 CFR 101.22 permits certain collective flavor/spice declarations but separately requires names for added MSG and protein hydrolysates. Applicable major-allergen labeling obligations still apply. The app does not verify that this database record or package meets those rules."],[["natural and artificial flavors","natural and artificial flavor","natural and artificial flavours","natural and artificial flavour","natural and artificial flavoring","natural and artificial flavouring","natural and artificial flavorings","natural and artificial flavourings","natural & artificial flavors","natural & artificial flavours","natural/artificial flavors","natural/artificial flavours"],"Mixed flavor declaration · components unspecified","The wording declares both natural and artificial flavor components. It does not establish their identities, proportions, or which contributes the characterizing flavor.","A declared flavor mixture. Neither a natural component nor an artificial component supplies a health verdict or independently verified source.","101.22",true,"US 21 CFR 101.22 permits certain collective flavor/spice declarations but separately requires names for added MSG and protein hydrolysates. Applicable major-allergen labeling obligations still apply. The app does not verify that this database record or package meets those rules."],[["flavor","flavors","flavour","flavours","flavoring","flavorings","flavouring","flavourings"],"Flavor · category unspecified","Generic flavor wording does not establish natural versus artificial category, chemical identities, or source materials. No category or hidden ingredient is inferred.","May contribute taste or aroma. The exact preparation and manufacturer's function are not verified by the generic word.","101.22",true,"US labeling rules distinguish flavor categories and characterizing-flavor claims. A generic database term is not proof of lawful or unlawful labeling in this product's market."],[["vanillin","4-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzaldehyde"],"Named flavor compound","Vanillin is a named aroma compound, not the same preparation as vanilla extract or ethyl vanillin. The name does not identify bean extraction, fermentation, or chemical manufacture.","May impart or reinforce vanilla-like aroma or taste. Compound identity does not establish vanilla-bean origin, a natural/artificial label classification, or a health benefit.","https://www.hfpappexternal.fda.gov/scripts/fdcc/index.cfm?set=FoodSubstances&id=VANILLIN",false,""],[["ethyl vanillin","ethylvanillin","3-ethoxy-4-hydroxybenzaldehyde"],"Named flavor compound","Ethyl vanillin is a different compound from vanillin and is not vanilla extract. Its actual production route and preparation are not established by the name.","May impart or reinforce vanilla-like flavor. The name does not establish concentration, manufacturer intent, or an individual health effect.","https://www.hfpappexternal.fda.gov/scripts/fdcc/index.cfm?set=FoodSubstances&id=ETHYLVANILLIN",false,""],[["vanilla extract","extract of vanilla"],"Vanilla extract preparation","US standardized vanilla extract is an aqueous ethyl-alcohol solution of flavor/aroma principles from vanilla beans. It is a mixture, not pure vanillin; the label does not independently verify conformance.","May contribute vanilla aroma and taste. Bean source, optional carriers/ingredients, amount used, and this food's residual alcohol remain unknown.","169.175",false,"US 21 CFR 169.175 specifies at least 35 percent ethyl alcohol by volume in conforming extract. That is not the alcohol percentage of a finished food containing it and does not prove compliance or alcohol-free status."],[["vanilla flavoring","vanilla flavouring"],"Vanilla flavoring preparation","The US standardized term is related to vanilla extract but has less than 35 percent ethyl alcohol by volume. It is not automatically alcohol-free, pure vanillin, or a generic vanilla-flavor description.","May contribute vanilla aroma and taste. The term does not measure residual alcohol in this food or establish the actual source/formulation.","169.177",false,"US 21 CFR 169.177 distinguishes standardized vanilla flavoring from vanilla extract. Other markets and informal database wording may differ; this entry is not a compliance certification."],[["spice","spices"],"Seasoning category · components unspecified","US rules define spices as qualifying aromatic vegetable substances used principally for seasoning. Generic wording does not identify each spice; spice extracts and essential oils are different preparations.","May contribute seasoning, aroma, or taste. Specific spices, amounts, and allergy relevance are not determined by the collective term.","101.22",true,"US 21 CFR 101.22 permits certain collective flavor/spice declarations but separately requires names for added MSG and protein hydrolysates. Applicable major-allergen labeling obligations still apply. The app does not verify that this database record or package meets those rules. US rules require foods such as onion, garlic, and celery to be named rather than hidden within the collective spice term."]];
